import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>1.4c — Slot Machine: Payouts &amp; Polish</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Your slot machine works, but it's basic. A real slot machine has different
        payout tiers, a running balance, and feels like a game — not a math problem.
        Time to expand it.
    </p>

    <h3>Requirement 1: Payout Tiers</h3>

    <p>Right now you have a binary "JACKPOT or nothing" system. Add these tiers:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Three match:</strong> JACKPOT — multiply bet by 10</li>
        <li><strong>Two match:</strong> Small win — multiply bet by 2</li>
        <li><strong>No match:</strong> Lose the bet</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Bug Hunt: The Pairing Problem</h3>
        <p>Here's a naive approach to checking for two-of-a-kind:</p>
        <pre><code>if (reel1 == reel2 || reel1 == reel3 || reel2 == reel3)</code></pre>
        <p>Run your slot machine with this check. Then run it again. And again.
        When three reels match, what happens? Does the program print BOTH
        "Small win!" AND "JACKPOT!"? What logic do you need to add to fix this?</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Requirement 2: Running Balance</h3>

    <p>Track a balance that persists between spins:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Start with 100 coins</li>
        <li>The player bets 10 coins per spin</li>
        <li>After each spin, show: bet, win/loss amount, new balance</li>
        <li>Game ends when balance reaches 0 — print a summary</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>You need the balance to survive across spins. Where in the program
                do you declare it? Why can't you put it inside the spin logic?</li>
            <li>Your payout tiers check three reels for equality. How many
                <code>if</code> statements did you write? Could you reduce them
                using a different approach?</li>
            <li>What happens when you bet 10 but your balance is 5? Should your
                program let that happen? How would you prevent it?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <h3>Requirement 3: Polish the Output</h3>

    <p>Make it look like a real game:</p>
    <pre><code><span class="output">═══════════════════════════
  SLOT MACHINE
  Balance: 85 coins
═══════════════════════════
  [ Cherry | Lemon | Cherry ]
  Two of a kind! You win 20 coins!
  New balance: 105 coins
═══════════════════════════</span></code></pre>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Push It Further (pick one)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Add a "double or nothing" option after a win — flip a coin (50% chance), double your winnings or lose it all</li>
            <li>Track total spins, total wins, and net profit. Print final stats when the player busts.</li>
            <li>Add a "Lucky 7" special payout: if any reel shows 7, return half the bet regardless of matching</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Implement multi-tier conditional logic (three match / two match / none)</li>
            <li>Track state that changes across multiple operations (running balance)</li>
            <li>Prevent overlapping conditionals (three-of-a-kind also triggers two-of-a-kind check)</li>
            <li>Format output into clean, readable game displays</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/slot-machine.html">Slot Machine Walkthrough</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/math-random.html">Math.random()</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/three-step-pattern.html">Three-Step Pattern</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
